  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "subtitle": "From 0 to 1000. Up to 30 most numbers are one word: dieciséis, veintidós. After that, use y: treinta y uno. Uno shortens before a noun: un euro, veintiún años, and it agrees with feminine nouns: una casa.",
  "briefMarks": ["uno", "un", "una", "veintiún", "cien", "ciento"],
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "16–29: one word", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "31–99: tens + y + ones", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "100: cien · 101: ciento uno" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "16 → dieciséis · 22 → veintidós · 31 → treinta y uno · 45 → cuarenta y cinco · 100 → cien · 150 → ciento cincuenta",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>16 to 29</strong> are one word: <em>dieciséis, diecisiete, veinte, veintiuno, veintidós, veintitrés</em>. Some have an accent: <em>dieciséis, veintidós, veintitrés, veintiséis</em>.",
        "tag": "16–29"
      },
      {
        "html": "From <strong>31</strong>, use three words with <strong>y</strong>: <em>treinta y uno, cuarenta y dos, noventa y nueve</em>. There is no y after the hundreds: <em>ciento cinco</em>, not <em>ciento y cinco</em>.",
        "tag": "31–99"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>uno</strong> changes before a noun: <em>un euro, una hora, veintiún años, veintiuna personas, treinta y un días</em>. On its own it stays <em>uno</em>: <em>¿Cuántos? – Uno.</em>",
        "tag": "uno, un, una"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>100</strong> alone or before a noun is <strong>cien</strong>: <em>cien euros</em>. From 101 it is <strong>ciento</strong>: <em>ciento veinte euros</em>. The hundreds agree: <em>doscientos euros, doscientas personas</em>. Learn <em>quinientos, setecientos, novecientos</em>.",
        "tag": "cien, ciento"
      },
      {
        "html": "In Spain, a comma marks decimals and a point marks thousands: <em>12,50 €</em> is <em>doce euros con cincuenta</em> or <em>doce cincuenta</em>. <em>1.250 €</em> is <em>mil doscientos cincuenta euros</em>.",
        "tag": "Prices"
      },
      {
        "html": "Phone numbers are usually said in groups, in twos or threes: <em>612 34 56 78</em> → <em>seis, doce; treinta y cuatro; cincuenta y seis; setenta y ocho</em>. You can always say digit by digit.",
        "tag": "Phone numbers"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>veintiuno euros</em> → ✓ <em>veintiún euros</em>. ✗ <em>ciento euros</em> → ✓ <em>cien euros</em>. ✗ <em>diez y seis</em> → ✓ <em>dieciséis</em>. ✗ <em>doscientos personas</em> → ✓ <em>doscientas personas</em>. ✗ <em>cincocientos</em> → ✓ <em>quinientos</em>. Use numbers with <a href=\"/prepositions-of-time\">the time</a>.",
    "reference": {
